    "result_text": "The build passes and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` flag so it's `true` when more than 80 owners have already been created for a given day, and `false` otherwise.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `bulkSignupWarning` read-only boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains `getBulkSignupWarning`/`setBulkSignupWarning`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added:\n   - `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80`.\n   - `exceedsBulkSignupThreshold(LocalDate)` \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the given date and returns whether that count is **greater than** 80 (null-safe).\n   - `toOwnerDtoWithBulkWarning(Owner)` \u2014 maps the owner and populates the flag.\n   - Wired this helper into `addOwner`, `getOwner`, and `listOwners` so every owner response carries an explicit `true`/`false` value.\n\nThis reuses the same registration-date accumulation path as the existing daily-limit rule (`requireDailyLimitNotReached`), consistent with the test's note that the two share the same counting path. The existing test (`coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold`, which creates one owner and asserts `bulkSignupWarning` is `false` via GET) passes, and `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
